as a biomarker of arsenic exposure: results from a prospective study</article-title><source>Toxicology</source><volume>225</volume><issue>2&#x02013;3</issue><fpage>225</fpage><lpage>233</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16860454</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b11-ehp-117-1059"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hall</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gamble</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Slavkovich</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Levy</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Cheng</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Determinants of arsenic metabolism: blood arsenic metabolites, plasma folate, cobalamin, and homocysteine concentrations in maternal-newborn pairs</article-title><source>Environ Health Perspect</source><volume>115</volume><fpage>1503</fpage><lpage>1509</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17938743</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-ehp-117-1059"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name><name><surname>Harper</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>A Native American exposure scenario</article-title><source>Risk Anal</source><volume>17</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>789</fpage><lpage>795</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9463932</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13-ehp-117-1059"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Huyck</surname><given-names>KL</given-names></name><name><surname>Kile</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Mahiuddin</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Quamruzzaman</surname><given-names>Q</given-names></name><name><surname>Rahman</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Breton</surname><given-names>CV</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Maternal arsenic exposure associated with low birth weight in Bangladesh</article-title><source>J Occup Environ Med</source><volume>49</volume><issue>10</issue><fpage>1097</fpage><lpage>1104</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18000415</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14-ehp-117-1059"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kaltreider</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Lariviere</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamilton</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Arsenic alters the function of the glucocorticoid receptor as a transcription factor</article-title><source>Environ Health Perspect</source><volume>109</volume><fpage>245</fpage><lpage>251</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11333185</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b15-ehp-117-1059"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kurttio</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Komulainen</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Hakala</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Kahelin</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Pekkanen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Urinary excretion of arsenic species after exposure to arsenic present in drinking water</article-title><source>Arch Environ Contam Toxicol</source><volume>34</volume><fpage>297</fpage><lpage>305</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9504979</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b16-ehp-117-1059"><mixed-citation publicatio